  "description": "Ver 0.1.2 allows passing a public key directly as a string to the ECDHAes encryption/decryption functions, with support for both compressed and uncompressed formats.\nVer 0.1.1 fixes a bug for ECDHAes. Ver 0.1.1 is not compatible with ver 0.1.0 when using ECDHAes.\nBitcoinSVCryptor ver 0.1.0 integrates bitcoin private/public keys with serval encryption methods, including ECDSA, ECC, ECDH and AES. IBE is in the plan for future version.",
